Knightly Arts Tradition Choice 1 - Warleader Sphere	CATEGORY:Knightly Arts Tradition Choice 1	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Conscript Martial Tradition,Martial Tradition - Knightly Arts	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Warleader Sphere
Martial Tradition - Knightly Arts	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Armor Training|Equipment - Knightly Training|Equipment - Shield Training	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Knightly Arts Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Training in the knightly arts includes learning how to wear and maneuver in chainmail, full plate, and other armor designed for warriors who fight in the vanguard, as well as learning how to wield weapons suitable for such combat. In addition, most knights are trained in horsemanship and the art of leadership. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Armor Training, Knightly Training, Shield Training Variable: Individuals trained in the Knightly Arts tradition gain either the Beastmastery sphere [ride] package, the Warleader sphere, or the Shield sphere as a bonus sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc39
Martial Tradition - Iron Breaker Style	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Open Hand Sphere|Berserker Sphere|Berserker - Greater Sunder	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Iron Breaker Style Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Eschewing weapons and armor as impediments on the path to self-perfection, students of the iron breaker style learn techniques to harden their bodies into living weapons. Open Hand sphere Berserker sphere, Greater Sunder Variable: Individuals trained in the Iron Breaker Style tradition gain either the Unarmored Training talent from the Equipment sphere or a talent from either the Berserker or Open Hand sphere as a bonus talent.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc37
Martial Tradition - Cunning Leader	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Fencing Sphere|Fencing - Expert Feint|Warleader Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Cunning Leader Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:The battlefield is an ever shifting place, causing chaos and anarchy to reign supreme. Only a cunning leader is able to properly navigate the terrain, commanding their troops while controlling the flow of combat in a way unique to them. Bonus Talents: Equipment: One [discipline] talent of their choice Fencing sphere, Expert Feint Warleader sphere	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc16
Martial Tradition - Pursuer	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Duelist Sphere|Scout Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Pursuer Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Pursuer Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:Bounty hunters, trackers, and ruthless assassins alike, a pursuer is a malicious and cruel combatant, harrying their foes with bleeding cuts and carefully placed strikes. Bonus Talents: Duelist Sphere Scout Sphere Variable: A pursuer gains one [discipline] talent of their choice from the Equipment sphere. Variable: A pursuer gains a talent of their choice from the Duelist or Scout sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc52
Martial Tradition - Weapon Master	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Dual Wielding Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Weapon Master Tradition Choice 1|2	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Weapon Master Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:Most warriors learn the art of combat in pursuit of a goal, such as serving in the army or to protect themselves while traveling. For the weapon master, mastery of combat is its own reward, and many will seek out exotic weapons and obscure disciplines simply for the joy of having learned them. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Weapon masters gain two discipline talents of their choice as bonus talents. Dual Wielding sphere Variable: Weapon masters gain a talent of their choice from the Dual Wielding sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc67
Martial Tradition - Gladiator	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Gladiator Training|Gladiator Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Gladiator Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Gladiator Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:Trained in the tradition of pure physical prowess, gladiators are known for their ability to overpower lesser combatants, imposing their will upon lesser warriors. There are many different varieties of gladiator, but all of them specialize in putting on shows worthy of an emperor. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Gladiator Training Gladiator sphere Variable: Gladiators gain either Armor Training, Shield Training, or Gladiator Training a second time from the Equipment sphere. Variable: Gladiators gain a talent of their choice from the Gladiator sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc31
Martial Tradition - Mixed Duelist	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Duelist Training|Dual Wielding Sphere|Dual Wielding - Impossible Reload|Dual Wielding - Mixed Assault	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	DESC:A popular tradition among reapers, mixed duelists use elegant melee weapons and pistols simultaneously to threaten their foes regardless of positioning. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Duelist Training Dual Wielding sphere, Impossible Reload, Mixed Assault	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc43
Martial Tradition - Phalanx Soldier	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Shield Training|Equipment - Spear Dancer|Shield Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Phalanx Soldier Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:The phalanx is a group of soldiers who combine spears and shields to create an impenetrable wall of death. Even when not flanked by their brothers-in-arms, a phalanx soldier is still a deadly force on any battlefield. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Shield Training, Spear Dancer Shield sphere Variable: Phalanx soldiers gain either Finesse Fighting from the Equipment sphere or a talent of their choice from the Shield sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc47
Martial Tradition - Pirate	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Pirate Training|Equipment - Unarmored Training|Fencing Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Pirate Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Pirates learn to fight on the decks of ships, where one must be both fast and light in order to avoid being shot or drowned. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Pirate Training, Unarmored Training Fencing sphere Variable: Pirates gain either the Duelist sphere or the Athletics sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc50
Martial Tradition - Gearhead	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Techmaniac|Equipment - Toolkit Training|Tech Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Gearhead Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Gearheads primarily utilize gadgets, guns, and other technological equipment in combat. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Techmaniac, Toolkit Training Tech sphere Variable: Gearheads gain either Tech Savvy from the Tech sphere, or the Trap sphere as a bonus talent.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc29
Martial Tradition - Animal Trainer	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Bounty Hunter’s Tools|Beastmastery Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	ABILITY:Spheres Beastmastery Package|AUTOMATIC|Beastmastery Package - Handle Animal	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Beastmastery Package|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Animal Trainer Tradition Choice 1|2	DESC:Animal trainers fight alongside tamed beasts, wielding the tools used for capturing and training their pets in battle. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Bounty Hunter’s Tools Beastmastery sphere [handle animal] package Variable: Animal trainers may select two additional talents, each chosen from either the Beastmastery sphere or the Equipment sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc4
Martial Tradition - Chemist	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Fast Draw|Alchemy Sphere|Barroom Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	ABILITY:Spheres Alchemy Package|AUTOMATIC|Alchemy Package - Formulae	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Alchemy Package|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Chemist Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Chemists who go adventuring often find the bottle makes as good of a weapon as what might be inside it. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Fast Draw Alchemy sphere [formulae package] Barroom sphere Variable: Chemists gain one additional talent of their choice from either the Barroom sphere or Alchemy sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc12
Martial Tradition - Commando	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Rogue Weapon Training|Leadership Sphere|Scout Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	ABILITY:Spheres Leadership Package|AUTOMATIC|Leadership Package - Cohort	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Leadership Package|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Commando Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Specialists that lead small groups in stealthy raids and sabotage. Bonus Talents Equipment: Rogue Weapon Training Leadership sphere [cohort] package Scout sphere Variable: Commandos gain a bonus talent from either the Equipment or Scout spheres.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc14
Martial Tradition - Militia	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Peasant Training|Beastmastery Sphere|Scout Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	ABILITY:Spheres Beastmastery Package|AUTOMATIC|Beastmastery Package - Handle Animal	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Beastmastery Package|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Militia Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Militias often rise in communities without the benefit of a formal military, where peasants of all stripes might one day have to take up arms in defense of their homes. While few militiamen have the benefits of formal war training, many are skilled at hunting, tracking, and handling animals, which can be quite handy in times of war. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Peasant Training Beastmastery sphere [handle animal] package Scout sphere Variable: Individuals with militia training gain an Equipment talent of their choice.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc42
Martial Tradition - Noble	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Duelist Training|Equipment - Finesse Fighting|Leadership Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	ABILITY:Spheres Leadership Package|AUTOMATIC|Leadership Package - Followers	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Leadership Package|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Noble Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Born to privilege and gifted with the time to pursue the art of personal combat. Bonus Talents Equipment: Duelist Training, Finesse Fighting Leadership sphere [follower] package Variable: Nobles gain a bonus talent from either the Duelist or Leadership spheres.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc46
Martial Tradition - Guild Training	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Finesse Fighting|Equipment - Rogue Weapon Training|Alchemy Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	ABILITY:Spheres Alchemy Package|AUTOMATIC|Alchemy Package - Poison	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Alchemy Package|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Guild Training Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:While many combatants learn their arts in courtyards, dojos, or monasteries, those who learn through criminal guilds tend to have many masters, none more cruel and informative than experience. Whether their skills are assembled through observing more experienced thieves and thugs, or beaten into them by uncaring assassins who care more for their guild’s reputation than the well-being of its members, the guild trained who survive their training are invariably deadly, fast, and cunning. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Finesse Fighting, Rogue Weapon Training Alchemy sphere [poison] package Variable: Individuals trained in the Guild Training tradition gain either the Fencing sphere or the Duelist sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc32
Martial Tradition - Steppe Rider	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Outrider Training|Equipment - Shortbow Mastery|Beastmastery Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	ABILITY:Spheres Beastmastery Package|AUTOMATIC|Beastmastery Package - Ride	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Beastmastery Package|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Steppe Rider Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Training on the harsh steppes breeds talented warriors. Whether fierce raiders or guarded nomads, steppe riders are trained in horseback archery, relying on precision and mobility in place of bulky armor or heavy melee weapons. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Outrider Training, Shortbow Mastery Beastmastery sphere [ride] package Variable: Steppe riders gain either the Barrage sphere or the Sniper sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc59
Martial Tradition - Ruin Delver	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Toolkit Training|Athletics Sphere|Athletics - Rope Swing	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	ABILITY:Spheres Athletics Package|AUTOMATIC|Athletics Package - Climb	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Athletics Package|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Ruin Delver Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Ruin delving requires quick wits and even quicker reflexes. With a backpack full of gear and a half-baked plan, ruin delvers live by the seat of their pants as they explore the leavings of past civilizations looking for what knowledge and artifacts they can recover. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Toolkit Training Athletics sphere [Climb] package, Rope Swing Variable: Ruin delvers gain a talent of their choice from the Equipment sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc55
Martial Tradition - All-Thrower	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Caber Toss|Equipment - Rock Toss|Berserker Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|All-Thrower Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:All-throwers are athletic warriors who specialize in sports that involve hurling large and cumbersome objects. Equipment: Caber Toss, Rock Toss Berserker sphere Variable: All-throwers gain either Barroom as a bonus sphere or the Barbaric Throw talent from the Berserker sphere as a bonus talent.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc3
Martial Tradition - Barbarian	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Tribal Training|Berserker Sphere|Scout Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Barbarian Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Barbarians are tribal warriors who cultivate their rage for use in combat. Skilled at both hunting and warfare, Barbarians are deadly, versatile fighters. Depending on the traditions of their tribe, a barbarian might fight alongside war animals or focus on their rage, breaking their weapons as often as their enemies with their mighty blows. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Tribal training Berserker sphere Scout sphere Variable: Barbarians gain either the Barroom sphere or the Beastmastery sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc6
Martial Tradition - Buccaneer	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Duelist Training|Equipment - Firearm Proficiency|Dual Wielding Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Buccaneer Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Most often found as hired company of pirates, buccaneers are fond of flashy and sometimes acrobatic combat, making themselves formidable foes in close quarters and at range. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Duelist Training, Firearm Proficiency Dual Wielding sphere Variable: Buccaneers gain either the Athletics sphere, Fencing sphere, or a Dual Wielding talent of their choice.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc8
Martial Tradition - Challenging Knight	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Armor Training|Equipment - Knightly Training|Gladiator Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Challenging Knight Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Unlike other knights, challenging knights are far more focused on their own personal glory, keeping combat and every other possible situation focused on themselves. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Armor Training, Knightly Training Gladiator sphere Variable: Individuals trained in the challenging knight gain either the Guardian sphere or a Gladiator talent of their choice.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc11
Martial Tradition - Courtesan	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Dancer Training|Equipment - Unarmored Training|Fencing Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Courtesan Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Courtesans are students of courtly manners and artistic pursuits, and are often experts at painting, dancing, music, and engaging conversation. In a world of magic and court intrigue, courtesans are often also trained as bodyguards and assassins. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Dancer Training, Unarmored Training Fencing sphere Variable: Courtesans gain either the Dual Wielding sphere or a talent from the Fencing sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc15
Martial Tradition - Crushing Juggernaut	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Armor Training|Brute Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Crushing Juggernaut Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Crushing Juggernaut Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:Crushing juggernauts specialize in using their bulk and the mass of their heavy armor to grind their opponents into dust. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Armor Training Brute sphere Variable: Crushing juggernauts gain a bonus talent of their choice from both the Brute sphere and the Equipment sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc17
Martial Tradition - Daring Scholar	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Staff Mastery|Alchemy Sphere|Scout Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Daring Scholar Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:While many adventurers train with weapons and armor to protect them from the dangers of their chosen lifestyle, others trust in their wits and ingenuity to keep them safe. Daring scholars use a combination of explosive chemical compounds and careful observation to overcome any challenge, considering a spyglass and an alchemist’s lab to be a preferable burden to a knight’s heavy plate. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Staff Mastery Alchemy sphere Scout sphere Variable: Daring scholars gain a talent from either the Alchemy or Scout sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc18
Martial Tradition - Decisive Fist	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Critical Genius|Boxing Sphere|Open Hand Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Decisive Fist Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Disciples of the decisive fist prefer to end fights with one powerful punch. These inspired combatants coil up like a spring, choosing the perfect moment to disrupt their foes with a brutal blow. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Critical Genius Boxing sphere Open Hand sphere Variable: Decisive fists gain either Finesse Fighting, Unarmed Training, or Unarmored Training from the Equipment sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc19
Martial Tradition - Dedicated Lancer	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Pikeman Training|Equipment - Spear Dancer|Lancer Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Dedicated Lancer Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Completely focused on their aims of goring opponents, dedicated lancers are masters of the spear, focusing on impaling foes and leaving them on the end of their weapon. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Pikeman Training, Spear Dancer Lancer sphere Variable: Individuals trained as Dedicated Lancers gain either the Guardian sphere or a Lancer talent of their choice.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc21
Martial Tradition - Drunken Brawler	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Unarmed Training|Barroom Sphere|Wrestling Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Drunken Brawler Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Only a “tradition” in the vaguest sense of the word, drunken brawlers tend to learn their arts at the hands of other drunken brawlers, usually through an alcohol induced fog while their “teacher” attempts to put them through a bar. Or a wall. Or a ceiling. Occasionally a door. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Unarmed Training Barroom sphere Wrestling sphere Variable: Drunken brawlers gain a talent of their choice from either the Barroom or Wrestling sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc22
Martial Tradition - Dual Blade Beast	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Dual Blade Savant|Dual Wielding Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Dual Blade Beast Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Dual Blade Beast Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:Not settling for an ordinary weapon, dual blade beasts focus on a more exotic weapon, using its modular nature in unique and interesting ways. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Bushido Training or Duelist Training, Dual Blade Savant Dual Wielding sphere Variable: Individuals trained in the Dual Blade Beast gain either the Duelist sphere or a Dual Wielding talent of their choice.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc23
Martial Tradition - Fearless Thrower	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Huntsman Training|Equipment - Throwing Mastery	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Fearless Thrower Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Fearless Thrower Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:From small blades to large spears, fearless throwers are adept at launching any such items into the air. Able to push the limits of thrown weapons far beyond what others can, they fill the air with a hail of knives, hammers, and spears. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Huntsman Training, Throwing Mastery Variable: Fearless throwers either gain Crushing Thrower or Thrower’s Reflexes from the Equipment sphere. Variable: Fearless throwers gain either the Barrage sphere or the Berserker sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc25
Martial Tradition - Giant	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Rock Toss|Brute Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Giant Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Giant Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:Creatures who are larger than their peers often learn to fight in fashions leveraging their enormous size, shoving their enemies around the battlefield and hurling objects far too large for their enemies to handle. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Rock Toss Brute sphere Variable: Giants gain a talent of their choice from both the Brute sphere and the Equipment sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc30
Martial Tradition - Professional Wrestler	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Unarmored Training|Gladiator Sphere|Wrestling Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Professional Wrestler Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Professional wrestlers are equal parts showman and combatant. Whether using pain-wracking joint locks or high-flying aerial maneuvers, these skilled individuals revel in their own physical might, relishing the applause that follows a particularly daring stunt. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Unarmored Training Gladiator sphere Wrestling sphere Variable: Professional wrestlers gain one talent of their choice from either the Wrestling sphere or the Gladiator sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc51
Martial Tradition - Retiarius	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Gladiator Training|Equipment - Net Master|Gladiator Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Retiarius Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:This specialized gladiator style typically combines net in order to disable foes before dispatching them with a single stab. While it was born in the arena, the tradition proves effective on the battlefield. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Gladiator Training, Net Master Gladiator sphere Variable: Individuals trained in the Retiarius tradition gain either the Duelist sphere or the Lancer sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc53
Martial Tradition - Rogue Gunner	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Firearm Proficiency|Equipment - Expert Reloading|Scoundrel Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Rogue Gunner Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Aware of the dangers of living on the streets, rogue gunners travel quick, fire fast, and leave anyone who would challenge them in a pool of blood. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Firearm Proficiency, Expert Reloading Scoundrel sphere Variable: Individuals trained in the Rogue Gunner gain either the Athletics sphere or a Scoundrel talent of their choice.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc54
Martial Tradition - Mechanic	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Expert Reloading|Trap Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Mechanic Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Mechanic Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:A mechanic is an engineer or craftsman adept at the working of machines and other complex systems. While not all engineers will go adventuring, those who do find their knowledge can be remarkably valuable to their allies. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Expert Reloading Trap sphere Variable: Mechanics gain either Firearm Proficiency or Mechanical Training from the Equipment sphere. Variable: Mechanics gain either the Barrage sphere or the Sniper sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc41
Martial Tradition - Warden	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Armor Training|Equipment - Shield Training|Guardian Sphere|Shield Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	DESC:The path of the warden is one of a stalwart protector, often employed as bodyguards or garrisoned soldiers. These warriors know that defense is the best offense, especially when you have friends to outflank your foes. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Armor Training, Shield Training Guardian sphere Shield sphere	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc66
Martial Tradition - Staff Master	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Finesse Fighting|Equipment - Spear Dancer|Equipment - Staff Mastery|Equipment - Unarmored Training	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	DESC:Whether they are magicians using magic staves as bludgeons or spearmen of exquisite skill, for some all that’s needed is speed and a stick to overcome most foes. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Finesse Fighting, Spear Dancer, Staff Mastery, Unarmored Training	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc58
Martial Tradition - Armored Dreadnought	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Armor Training|Equipment - Shield Training	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Armored Dreadnought Tradition Choice 1|2	DESC:Armored Dreadnoughts specialize in wielding massive shields and titanic suits of armor that would crush lesser men under their enormous weight. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Armor Training, Shield Training Variable: Armored dreadnoughts gains two talents of their choice from the Equipment sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc5
Martial Tradition - Combat Gunner	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Firearm Proficiency|Equipment - Gun Kata|Open Hand Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Combat Gunner Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Guns aren’t the most friendly of weapons, making the efforts of combat gunners all the more impressive. Willing to duck and weave into melee combat as well as fire from a distance, these masters of close and long range combat lack any fear. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Firearm Proficiency, Gun Kata Open Hand sphere Variable: Combat gunners gain either Barrage sphere or Sniper sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc13
Martial Tradition - Monastic Path	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Monk Weapon Training|Equipment - Staff Mastery|Open Hand Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Monastic Path Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Those who would seek enlightenment through contemplation hone their bodies and minds alike. Followers of the monastic path train with a wide variety of challenging weapons, learning truths in every new combat technique and finding greater mysteries as they stretch their boundaries. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Monk Weapon Training, Staff Mastery Open Hand sphere Variable: Individuals trained in the Monastic Path tradition gain either the Athletics sphere or the Dual Wielding sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc44
Martial Tradition - Ninjutsu	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Finesse Fighting|Equipment - Monk Weapon Training|Scoundrel Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Ninjutsu Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Shadowy warriors learn underhanded combat styles, using everything at their disposal to level the playing field against superior forces. Those trained in ninjutsu combine grace with subterfuge, confident in the knowledge that disrupting their opponents shall defeat them even before blood is shed. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Finesse Fighting, Monk Weapon Training Scoundrel sphere Variable: Individuals trained in the Ninjutsu tradition gain either the Scout sphere or the Trap sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc45
Martial Tradition - Canny Hunter	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Huntsman Training|Scout Sphere|Sniper Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Canny Hunter Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Canny hunters are skilled marksmen and trackers, capable of spotting a creature’s weaknesses and felling them with a single well placed shot. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Huntsman Training Scout sphere Sniper sphere Variable: Canny hunters gain one additional talent of their choice from either the Equipment sphere or Scout sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc10
Martial Tradition - Heavy Armsman	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Dwarven Heritage|Equipment - Armor Training|Berserker Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Heavy Armsman Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:A heavy armsman specializes in using hammers, axes, and other large weapons to bring down even larger foes. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Dwarven Heritage, Armor Training Berserker sphere Variable: Individuals trained in the Heavy Armsman tradition gain one Equipment or Berserker talent of their choice.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc34
Martial Tradition - Pit Fighter	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Unarmed Training|Boxing Sphere|Gladiator Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Pit Fighter Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Like the gladiator or professional wrestler, the pit fighter puts on shows for money. However, unlike those other prize fighters, in the pits there are few grand traditions and even fewer rules; whoever’s alive at the end of the match is the winner. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Unarmed Training Boxing sphere Gladiator sphere Variable: Pit fighters gain one talent of their choice from either the Boxing sphere or the Gladiator sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc49
Martial Tradition - Street Fighter	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Unarmed Training|Brute Sphere|Scoundrel Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Street Fighter Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Street fighters learn combat in fights with no rules; where fakeouts and a handful of sand are all that stand between winning and losing. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Unarmed Training Brute sphere Scoundrel sphere Variable: Street fighters gain a talent of their choice from either the Brute sphere or the Scoundrel sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc61
Martial Tradition - Stone Thrower	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Halfling Heritage|Equipment - Sling Combatant|Barrage Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Stone Thrower Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Masters of the humble sling learn that versatility is key to survival, and a skilled stone thrower quickly learns to use their slings in almost any situation, making them deadly at any range. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Halfling Heritage, Sling Combatant Barrage sphere Variable: Stone throwers gain a talent of their choice from the Barrage sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc60
Martial Tradition - Thief	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Rogue Weapon Training|Scoundrel Sphere|Fencing Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Thief Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Thieves avoid fair fights whenever possible. Their favorite tactic is to take their opponents unaware, but barring that, a dirty trick or a well-placed feint will let them end the fight quickly. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Rogue Weapon Training Scoundrel sphere Fencing sphere Variable: Thieves gain either an Equipment talent of their choice, or a talent from the Scoundrel or Fencing spheres.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc63
Martial Tradition - Dedicated Duelist	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Duelist Training|Equipment - Finesse Fighting	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Dedicated Duelist Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Dedicated Duelist Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:Dedicated duelists are individuals devoted to the art of the duel. Whether they simply revel in the art of single combat, or if they believe that they can prevent larger battles by risking their life alone, these deadly men and women are focused and skilled in the tools of their chosen trade. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Duelist Training, Finesse Fighting Variable: Dedicated duelists gain either the Duelist sphere or Fencing sphere Variable: Dedicated duelists gain either Gauntlet Shield or Unarmored Training from the Equipment sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc20
Martial Tradition - Bolt Juggler	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Mechanical Training|Dual Wielding Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Bolt Juggler Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Bolt Juggler Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:Bolt jugglers are a sight to behold, awe-inspiring on the training ground and dread-inspiring on the battleground. While some use their crossbows to compliment a melee weapon, others wield two crossbows at once in a dizzying display of coordination. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Mechanical Training Dual Wielding sphere Variable: Bolt jugglers gain either Expert Reloading or Mechanical Savant from the Equipment sphere. Variable: Bolt jugglers gain either Impossible Reload or Mixed Assault from the Dual Wielding sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc7
Martial Tradition - Pikeman	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Pikeman Training|Equipment - Polearm Mastery|Lancer Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Pikeman Tradition Choice 1|1	DESC:Pikemen are soldiers who specialize in using polearms to take down enemy cavalry and to keep enemies at a safe distance. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Pikeman Training, Polearm Mastery Lancer sphere Variable: Pikemen gain either the Guardian sphere or a talent of their choice from the Lancer sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc48
Martial Tradition - Shield Master	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Shield Training|Shield Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Shield Master Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Shield Master Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:Shield masters are expert defenders, relying on their shields to defend both themselves and their allies. While some shield masters couple their shields with traditional weapons, others focus so exclusively on their shields that they become as much a weapon as a tool of defense, instead relying on brute force to knock their enemies around the battlefield and keep their allies out of danger. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Shield Training Shield sphere Variable: Shield masters gain either the Brute sphere or a talent of their choice from the Equipment sphere. Variable: Shield masters gain a talent of their choice from the Shield sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc57
Martial Tradition - Tempest Dancer	CATEGORY:Conscript Martial Tradition	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_CONSCRIPT_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Spheres Martial Focus	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment - Double Weapon Training|Dual Wielding Sphere	ABILITY:Spheres Combat Talent|AUTOMATIC|Equipment Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Spheres Equipment Bonus Talent|-1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Tempest Dancer Tradition Choice 1|1	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Tempest Dancer Tradition Choice 2|1	DESC:Wielding double-bladed weapons that others find impossible to master, tempest dancers are known for their ability to carve through through enemy ranks, their fluid movements beguiling even the most observant opponents. Bonus Talents: Equipment: Double Weapon Training Dual Wielding sphere Variable: Tempest dancers gain either the Armor Training, Unarmored Training, or Finesse Fighting from the Equipment sphere. Variable: Tempest Dancers gain a talent of their choice from the Dual Wielding sphere	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/martial-traditions#toc64
